{
  "_": [
    "munsters_pro on Allknowing2012's 'Munsters (Original 2020)' 1.05 (VPUniverse 10068;",
    "cGameName mmunsters), a scripted original on the same framework as his Aerosmith:",
    "vpxshadow.py keeps its script as a shadow game and hands the ball to the real game.",
    "The Pro, not the LE: the table has no lower playfield (the LE's second flippers,",
    "trough, VUK and ramp), no moving Herman and no Herman 2-bank targets (PAD-1095).",
    "The author named his switches by Stern's manual numbers (swNN = switch_list's `num`",
    "NN), so every switch below is matched by NAME; sw28 and sw31 are the Walls behind",
    "the Dragula and Lily targets. Ids: the RIG's switch_list.txt for munsters_pro; coils",
    "through group_node.txt (group 6 = node 8, group 7 = node 9).",
    "Mechs: the Dragula car is a Plunger (CarPlunger) the DRAGULA KICKER coil fires over",
    "sw29; the UP POST is the DropStop wall; TRAP DOOR-SPOT is SpotWall (RaiseSpot /",
    "DropSpot); MAGNET is mHMagnet; GRANDPA EJECT is the ScoopEject saucer.",
    "PinUP: the table creates PinUP Player in an On Error block but reads getroot and",
    "GetTimes(objFs.GetFolder(...)) outside it, so PadNoPuP stands in (pup_stub) and the",
    "GetTimes line is neutered. Lamps: the inserts by what the script does with them",
    "(each group's lighting order: Dragula L32 first, Lily L40, Spot L106/L89, Herman",
    "L58, Raven L95) and the rest by place; GUESS = wants a look at the machine.",
    "quiet_subs: its light shows, GI and lane change, which the machine does itself, and",
    "the triggers that would move the up post or light the ball save behind its back."
  ],
